<%- include('_partials/head', { pageStyles: ['/css/kurukoo-channel-page.css'] }) %>
<%- include('_partials/nav') %>
<main class="container page-container">
  <section class="page-header-center"><span class="badge-pill">Channels</span><h1 class="page-title">One Kurukoo relationship, different access points.</h1><p class="page-desc">Use the access point that is actually connected. Web Chat is active in this deployment; other channels are represented for future activation and are not presented as live until their adapters are configured.</p></section>
  <section class="channel-group"><h2 class="channel-group-title">Available now</h2><div class="channel-cards"><article class="channel-card available"><div class="channel-icon">W</div><span class="channel-state active">Available now</span><h3>Web Chat</h3><p>Start a conversation, review request details, manage reminders and continue protected actions when identity is required.</p><a href="/chat" class="btn btn-primary btn-sm">Start chatting</a></article></div></section>
  <section class="channel-group"><h2 class="channel-group-title">Other access points</h2><p class="channel-note">These channels are not connected in the current deployment. The connection setup is shown so the product can grow into them without creating separate user accounts or conversation systems.</p><div class="channel-cards">
    <article id="whatsapp" class="channel-card unavailable"><div class="channel-icon">WA</div><span class="channel-state">Not connected</span><h3>WhatsApp</h3><p>Kurukoo will use the same underlying conversation and account relationship when a verified WhatsApp adapter is enabled.</p><button class="btn btn-outline btn-sm" disabled>Connection coming soon</button><div class="channel-setup"><strong>Future setup</strong>Kurukoo would ask whether you want to connect WhatsApp, collect the required account details, then return a verified connection confirmation.</div></article>
    <article id="telegram" class="channel-card unavailable"><div class="channel-icon">TG</div><span class="channel-state">Not connected</span><h3>Telegram</h3><p>Telegram is represented as a future access point and is not active in this deployment.</p><button class="btn btn-outline btn-sm" disabled>Connection coming soon</button><div class="channel-setup"><strong>Future setup</strong>The connection flow will keep the same Kurukoo profile and conversation semantics.</div></article>
    <article id="sms" class="channel-card unavailable"><div class="channel-icon">SMS</div><span class="channel-state">Not connected</span><h3>SMS</h3><p>SMS notifications or conversations require a configured carrier and messaging adapter.</p><button class="btn btn-outline btn-sm" disabled>Connection coming soon</button><div class="channel-setup"><strong>Future setup</strong>Kurukoo would confirm the number and supported message permissions before activation.</div></article>
    <article id="ussd" class="channel-card unavailable"><div class="channel-icon">US</div><span class="channel-state">Not connected</span><h3>USSD</h3><p>USSD requires a configured carrier route and is not represented as a working public dial code here.</p><button class="btn btn-outline btn-sm" disabled>Connection coming soon</button><div class="channel-setup"><strong>Future setup</strong>The same request semantics would be adapted to a constrained menu interaction.</div></article>
  </div></section>
</main>
